measurements were collected at intervals of $^\mathrm{~2~h~}$ , and samples for rejection evaluation were taken once steady state was reached $\left(\mathbf{12}~\mathrm{h}\right)$ . The MWCO (molecular weight cut-off) was determined by interpolating from the plot of rejection against molecular weight of the above mentioned oligomers, and corresponds to the molecular weight for which rejection is $90\%$ .
Solvent flux (J) was determined by measuring permeate volume (V) per unit area (A) per unit time (t) according to the following equation (1):
$$
\textstyle{\mathrm{J}}={\frac{V}{A\cdot t}}
$$
The rejection (R ) of markers was calculated from Eq. (2), where $\mathbf{C}_{\mathrm{P,i}}$ and ${\bf C}_{\mathrm{F,i}}$ correspond to marker concentrations in the permeate and the feed, respectively.
$$
\begin{array}{r}{R_{i}=\left(1-\frac{C_{P,i}}{C_{F,i}}\right)\cdot100\%}\end{array}
$$
